    <div class="lux-brand-news-sheet"><header><p class="lux-brand-news-meta"><span>October 26, 2026</span><span>Event Review</span><span>LuxurEat</span></p><h1 id="lux-reader-title">From Lazio to Global Markets | LuxurEat China and Ugolini Group at SIAL Paris 2026</h1><p class="lux-brand-news-intro">SIAL Paris 2026 provided an international stage connecting Italian food excellence with global markets.</p><a class="lux-brand-news-source" href="https://www.sialparis.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SIAL Paris official website ↗</a></header><div class="lux-brand-news-copy"><p>SIAL Paris 2026 once again provided an important international stage connecting Italian food excellence with global markets. Representing one of Italy’s distinctive agri-food regions, Lazio brought 17 producers — including 16 companies and one cooperative — to the exhibition, showcasing the quality, tradition and innovation of the region’s food industry to an international professional audience.</p><p>With around 8,000 exhibitors and approximately 295,000 industry professionals expected to attend, SIAL Paris offers a major platform for food companies to connect with international buyers, distributors and business partners.</p><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>From Italy to the Chinese Market</h2><p>For Ugolini Group and LuxurEat China, SIAL Paris is more than an opportunity to showcase brands and products. It is an important meeting point between Italian producers and international markets.</p><p>Ugolini Group is committed to bringing distinctive Italian food products and culinary culture to a wider global audience, while LuxurEat China extends this vision towards the Chinese market, creating a bridge between Italian brands and Chinese consumers, buyers and business partners.</p><p>Through international trade fairs such as SIAL Paris, we can engage directly with buyers, distributors and professionals from different markets, better understand evolving consumer demand and explore new opportunities for commercial cooperation and distribution.</p><figure class="lux-brand-news-media is-video"><video controls playsinline webkit-playsinline preload="metadata" width="720" height="1280" poster="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/brand-news/sial-paris-2026-arsial-poster.webp'); ?>"><source src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/brand-news/sial-paris-2026-arsial.mp4'); ?>" type="video/mp4"></video><figcaption>Video source: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/arsial.lazio/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">arsial.lazio</a></figcaption></figure></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Bringing Lazio’s Food Industry to the World</h2><p>Throughout 2026, the Lazio Region has continued to support the international development of its agri-food sector, with approximately €3.7 million invested in a promotional programme covering more than 20 national and international trade events.</p><p>SIAL Paris represents an important part of this internationalisation strategy. For Lazio-based food businesses, including Ugolini Group, these events are not only showcases for their products, but also opportunities to establish lasting relationships across the global food industry.</p><p>This year’s programme also highlighted gluten-free products and more inclusive food choices through a collaboration with AIC Lazio, the Italian Coeliac Association’s Lazio branch. Show cooking sessions and tastings brought together quality, flavour and attention to increasingly diverse dietary needs.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Bringing Italian Flavours Further</h2><p>From Lazio to Paris, and from Italy to China, internationalisation is not simply about entering new markets — it is about creating new connections.</p><p>Building on Ugolini Group’s experience in Italian food and LuxurEat China’s growing presence in the Chinese market, our goal is to introduce more consumers, buyers and partners to quality Italian food while creating new opportunities for Italian brands to connect with China.</p><p>SIAL Paris 2026 represents another important step in this journey — and a new starting point for strengthening the connection between Italian food excellence and international markets.</p></section><a class="lux-brand-news-event-link" href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/brand', '#event-sial-paris-2026')); ?>"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/events/sial-paris-2026-160.webp'); ?>" alt=""><span><small>Exhibitions &amp; Events</small><strong>SIAL Paris 2026 | Paris, Here We Come! 🇫🇷</strong></span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
  </article></main>
